king guidance and resources related to allergies and food intolerances.\",2\r\n14050,PRICK TEST,Prueba cutánea utilizada para diagnosticar alergias alimentarias mediadas por IgE mediante la aplicación de un alérgeno en la epidermis.,2\r\n14051,RAST,\"Prueba in vitro que determina la existencia de IgE específicas mediante radioinmunoensayo, útil para diagnosticar alergias alimentarias.\",2\r\n11820,REACCIONES ALÉRGICAS,\"\"\"REACCIONES ALÉRGICAS\"\" refer to immune responses that occur when the body reacts to substances it perceives as harmful, known as allergens. These reactions often involve the release of histamine and can vary in severity and type of symptoms. The immune system's response to these allergens can manifest in various ways, highlighting the diverse nature of allergic reactions.\",2\r\n14025,ANTICUERPOS IGG,\"Los anticuerpos IgG son un tipo de anticuerpo que puede indicar exposición a ciertos alimentos, pero no necesariamente una reacción alérgica.\",1\r\n516,PACIENTES EXTRAESOFÁGICOS,\"Extraesophageal patients are individuals experiencing symptoms related to reflux that are not confined to the esophagus, such as cough or hoarseness.\",1\r\n515,REFLUJO PATOLÓGICO NO ÁCIDO,\"Pathological non-acid reflux refers to reflux episodes that do not involve acidic content, which can be assessed through pH-impedance testing.\",1\r\n5949,SÍNDROMA DE DUMPING,,1\r\n14081,ALERGIA INFANTILLA FE,ALERGIA INFANTILLA FE is an organization dedicated to addressing childhood allergies and providing relevant resources.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3647,SÍNTOMAS,DIABETES,Symptoms are key indicators of diabetes and are crucial for early diagnosis and management of the disease.,175\r\n3653,SÍNTOMAS,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"Symptoms of cancer can lead to malnutrition, necessitating nutritional support\",116\r\n3650,SÍNTOMAS,DIETA CETOGÉNICA,Los síntomas como fatiga y debilidad muscular pueden aparecer en pacientes que sig